        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eb10a2ea-d642-5e66-b66f-beb8faa547b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Oera Linda Book\n- People: Friso, Martinus Hamconius, Alexander the Great\n- Languages: Old Frisian\n- Places: Punjab, Rhine, Weser, European North Sea coast\n- Topics: Frisian colonists, historical mythology\n\nFacts:\n- The Oera Linda Book is a manuscript written in a form of Old Frisian.\n- The Oera Linda Book purports to cover historical, mythological, and religious themes from 2194 BCE to 803 CE.\n- Old Frisian is a West Germanic language spoken between the 8th and 16th centuries.\n- Old Frisian was spoken in the area between the Rhine and Weser on the European North Sea coast.\n- In the 17th century, Martinus Hamconius wrote the chronicle \"Frisia seu de viris rebusque illustribus\".\n- According to Martinus Hamconius's chronicle and the 19th century Oera Linda Book, Friso was a leader of Frisian colonists in the Punjab.\n- According to those sources, Friso's group had been settled in the Punjab for well over a millennium when Alexander the Great discovered them.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
